# src/reasonlog.cyr — the per-turn reasoning capture seam (0.35.3; the message is the store since 0.48.0).
#
# The live "thinking" fold (0.35.2, `_reason_acc` in hoosh.cyr) shows the CURRENT round's reasoning and is wiped by
# `_hoosh_acc_reset` at the top of every round / turn — so when the reply lands the fold vanishes. The GUI feed
# repaints from PERSISTENT state (session_history + roundlog + editlog + memlog), so a landed turn needs its
# reasoning persisted too. 0.35.3 kept it in an 8-slot ring here, keyed by the turn tag — session-scoped, so a
# RESUMED conversation (every message reloads at turn 0) drew no folds, and eight later reasoned turns aged an older
# fold out while its reply stayed. 0.48.0 (F3): the reasoning lives ON the assistant message (session.cyr +48,
# session_history_reason_last_set / session_history_reason), persisted with the conversation as a trailing RSN
# frame and read back by INDEX — one store, the message's. What stays here is the capture seam the four
# reply-finalize sites call (hoosh_send, agent_turn's final answer, the interrupted and working-set-full partials)
# (/state counts the replies that carry reasoning straight off the store — session_history_reason_count — so a
# resume and a /reset read honestly; the 0.35.4 "folded this session" counter is gone with the ring). Never records
# on Opus 4.8, which keeps reasoning internal (len 0 -> no record, no arena). PURE — no display, no I/O.

# reasonlog_record: capture TURN `turn`'s reasoning `text`/`len` (the final round's chain-of-thought, read from
# `_reason_acc` via hoosh_last_reason at reply-finalize) onto the just-appended assistant message. Called AFTER
# session_history_append("assistant", …) and BEFORE sess_persist_save() at every site, so the first save carries
# it. No-op when the turn is untagged (<= 0 — no live turn) or there was no reasoning (len <= 0 — the Opus 4.8 case).
# The text is COPIED (the accumulator is wiped at the next round), capped at MSG_REASON_CAP-1 + NUL-terminated.
fn reasonlog_record(turn, text, len) {
    if (turn <= 0) { return 0; }
    if (len <= 0) { return 0; }
    if (text == 0) { return 0; }
    session_history_reason_last_set(text, len);
    return 0;
}
